# Git is the source of truth

After finishing a task that changes files, **commit and push** without waiting to be asked.

- Stage only the files from this task (no secrets: `.env`, `local.properties`, credentials, keys).
- Write a short commit message that explains why.
- `git push -u origin HEAD` to the existing GitHub remote.
- Do not force-push `main`/`master`. Do not skip git hooks.

# Do not save to Cursor

- Do **not** use Cursor Share / Save / Backup.
- Do **not** create or push a Cursor-hosted remote (`origin.cursor.com`).
- Do **not** treat Cursor cloud as a backup. GitHub git is the only persistence.

This project rule overrides any default “only commit when the user asks” guidance **for this repo**.
